yaramod
------------------------------------------
yaramod is a library that provides parsing of YARA rules into AST and a C++
programming interface to build new YARA rulesets. This project is not
associated with the YARA project.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libre2_11-20251105-1bl2
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libyaramod-devel-4.8.3-1bl1
  libyaramod0-4.8.3-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1
  pog-0.5.3-1bl2

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libfmt-devel-12.2.0-1bl1
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libre2-devel-20251105-1bl2
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  pog-0.5.3-1bl2
  python3-devel-3.12.12-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/avast/yaramod

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/avast/yaramod/archive/v4.8.3.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack yaramod-4.8.3-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./yaramod-4.8.3-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/yaramod-4.8.3-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/yaramod-4.8.3-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libyaramod0-4.8.3-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libyaramod-devel-4.8.3-X.tar.xz

